      "writtenOn": "2016-12-21T18:57:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "in case of in_len \u003d\u003d 0, pkcs1_type1_pad will still work fine.\n1) in_len \u003d\u003d 0 is allowed only for hash_size \u003d\u003d 0, i.e. for the \"padding-only\" case when we sign anything that fits into padded_len, not just buffers of size equal to the hashing algorithm digest size.\n2) and for padding-only case, if in_len \u003d\u003d 0, the entire buffer is just padding, so it\u0027s ok.\n\nAs for in_len \u003e SHA_MAX_DIGEST_BYTES, again, we care only that the data-to-sign fits in the buffer. And this is checked in the next statement after this if():\nif (in_len \u003e padded_len - RSA_PKCS1_PADDING_SIZE - der_size)\n\treturn 0;",
      "parentUuid": "5a7fdbe6_4c129478",
